This change initializes `course` to `null`, then renders a loading indicator while data is fetched. When the data is retrieved, `setCourseDetail` updates the state.  After the data is fetched, a check `if (!course)` is performed which, if true, causes the component to render nothing (or a dedicated 'Not Found' component). Finally, the component uses `course` instead of `courseDetail` directly in the JSX render.  This prevents the rendering of an empty element before the data has been retrieved.
